    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d323">

                <pb facs="0449" n="367" sameAs="frus:frus1925v02/pg367"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.6176 F 51/75</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chief of the Division of Western European
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Castle</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-04-08"><hi rendition="#italic">April 8,
                        1924</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">The Secretary</hi>: I had a talk late yesterday
                    afternoon with Mr. Hines, Secretary of the Firestone Company.</p>
                <p>He tells me that the reports brought by their agents from Liberia are very
                    optimistic and that Mr. Firestone, unless something unforeseen occurs, is
                    planning within the next two months to draw up a suggestion for a substantial
                    loan [and] to make a proposition to the Liberian Government. His aim is to use
                    this money so far as possible to build up the country in the way it was planned
                    to do under the old government loan.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d323-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed>W. R. C[<hi rendition="#small-caps">astle</hi>,]
                    Jr.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d323-f1" n="1" xml:id="d323-f1-content">
                <p>For correspondence concerning the proposed Government loan, see <ref
                        target="frus1920v03#pg_49"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>,
                        1920, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">iii</hi>, pp. 49</ref> ff.; <ref
                        target="frus1921v02#pg_368">1921, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>,
                        pp. 368</ref> ff.; and <ref target="frus1922v02#pg_606">1922, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>, pp. 606</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
